{"id":"27318d1875d83624","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-cor-gch.md","title":"Generalized CH Corollary","display":"cor-gch — Generalized CH Corollary","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-gch","aliases":["58-cor-gch","58-cor-gch-borel","GCH Borel Corollary"],"display":"cor-gch — Generalized CH Corollary","depends_on":["[[58-df-gch]]","[[58-df-constructible-universe]]","[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-gch"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-gch</span><span>58-cor-gch-borel</span><span>GCH Borel Corollary</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-gch — Generalized CH Corollary"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" href=\"?note=f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" title=\"58-df-gch\">58-df-gch</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"de47935b5769dd1e\" href=\"?note=de47935b5769dd1e\" title=\"58-df-constructible-universe\">58-df-constructible-universe</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bdf91bc7ddbdd903\" href=\"?note=bdf91bc7ddbdd903\" title=\"58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH\">58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\">\\(L\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\)</span> (the constructible-universe class, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"de47935b5769dd1e\" href=\"?note=de47935b5769dd1e\" title=\"58-df-constructible-universe\">58-df-constructible-universe</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> (generalized continuum hypothesis, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" href=\"?note=f13d4bbe06c4eb5a\" title=\"58-df-gch\">58-df-gch</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(L\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> (metatheoretic truth in the proper-class structure <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(L,\\in)\">\\((L,\\in)\\)</span>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}gch}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}L\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{GCH}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}gch}\\vdash_{\\mathsf{meta}}L\\models_{\\mathsf{meta}}\\mathrm{GCH}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>In the constructible universe <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>, the generalized continuum hypothesis holds.</li>\n<li>The corollary reuses the registered GCH proposition and proper-class satisfaction theorem; the former undefined abbreviation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}_L\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}_L\\)</span> has been removed.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> is the canonical inner model of ZFC + GCH.</li>\n<li><code>58-cor-gch-borel</code> is merged here; it asserted the same <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L \\models \\mathrm{GCH}\">\\(L \\models \\mathrm{GCH}\\)</span> consequence.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-gch","status":"resolved","id":"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-gch]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-constructible-universe","status":"resolved","id":"de47935b5769dd1e","anchor":"ref-2","targetAn